---
source: crates/standalone/fixture/src/lib.rs
---
Take a site down.

\e[1mUsage\e[0m: \e[1m\e[36mink\e[0m \e[1m\e[36mabuse\e[0m \e[1m\e[36msuspend\e[0m \e[36m[OPTIONS]\e[0m \e[36m<SITE>\e[0m

\e[1mExamples\e[0m
  \e[2m# \e[0mTake the site down, naming the report that led to it
  \e[1m\e[36mink\e[0m \e[1m\e[36mabuse\e[0m \e[1m\e[36msuspend\e[0m 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef \e[1m\e[36m--kind\e[0m phishing \e[1m\e[36m--report\e[0m fedcba9876543210fedcba9876543210

\e[1mArguments\e[0m
  \e[36m<SITE>\e[0m  The site's id, as `\e[1m\e[36mink\e[0m \e[1m\e[36mabuse\e[0m \e[1m\e[36mlist\e[0m` or the site's owner gives it

\e[1mOptions\e[0m
  \e[1m\e[36m    --kind\e[0m \e[36m<KIND>\e[0m  Why: phishing, malware, illegal, impersonation, spam or
                     other \e[2m[default: other]\e[0m
  \e[1m\e[36m    --report\e[0m \e[36m<ID>\e[0m  The report that led to it, as `\e[1m\e[36mink\e[0m \e[1m\e[36mabuse\e[0m \e[1m\e[36mlist\e[0m` shows its id

\e[1mAccount\e[0m
  \e[1m\e[36m    --api\e[0m \e[36m<URL>\e[0m          The API's address, `\e[1m\e[36mhttp://host[:port]\e[0m`;
                           `\e[1m\e[36maccount.api\e[0m` in the config file \e[2m[env: INK_API]\e[0m
  \e[1m\e[36m    --timeout\e[0m \e[36m<SECONDS>\e[0m  Seconds one call may take \e[2m[default: 30]\e[0m
                           \e[2m[env: INK_TIMEOUT]\e[0m

\e[1mNotes\e[0m
  A suspended site serves a notice and takes no deploy, build or change; its
  files stay and come back whole when the suspension is lifted. Only the
  operator's key may do this: it is the key `\e[1m\e[36mink\e[0m \e[1m\e[36mlogin\e[0m \e[1m\e[36m--data\e[0m` made.

\e[1mExit codes\e[0m
  0  Done
  2  Wrong usage: no API named, a key that is none, a private key that would
     print to a terminal
  3  No key, or the API refused the signature, or nobody approved the key in
     time
  4  The API could not be reached or failed; safe to retry

\e[1mEnvironment\e[0m
  \e[1m\e[36mINK_API\e[0m       The address of the API, as --api
  \e[1m\e[36mINK_SITE\e[0m      The site's id, as --site
  \e[1m\e[36mINK_KEY\e[0m       The private key to sign requests with, for a CI job; never a
                flag, so it stays out of process lists. `\e[1m\e[36mink\e[0m \e[1m\e[36mlogin\e[0m` keeps one in
                the config folder instead
  \e[1m\e[36mINK_KEY_FILE\e[0m  A file that holds that key, in place of INK_KEY

\e[2mDocs\e[0m    \e[4m\e[36mhttps://github.com/uses-ink/uses.ink/blob/main/docs/cli.md\e[0m
\e[2mGlobal\e[0m  \e[1m\e[36m-C,\e[0m \e[1m\e[36m--json,\e[0m \e[1m\e[36m-q,\e[0m \e[1m\e[36m-v,\e[0m \e[1m\e[36m--color,\e[0m \e[1m\e[36m--no-progress,\e[0m \e[1m\e[36m--log,\e[0m \e[1m\e[36m--log-file\e[0m
        \e[2m(see `ink --help`)\e[0m
